{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/796872-c-td20-the-black-compendium-what-a-strectch-goal-it-would-be","id":796872,"title":"C:tD20 -- The Black Compendium: What a strectch goal it would be!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-30T09:51:32-08:00","id":796872,"title":"C:tD20 -- The Black Compendium: What a strectch goal it would be!","content":"I wanted to repeat here that my dream for a future reward would be a Book of Nod-style book for Changeling, because the game line didn't get one, and it is time.<br /> <br /> I would call it the Book of Compendia, because it would give us the Black Compendium in its entirety (or at least the known fragments): narrating the founding of Arcadia, the War of Trees and the subsequent departure of the Tuatha d\u00e9 Danaan for the Far Shores. It would tell us of the victory against the White City of Bones, after their White Fomorian lords had imprisoned a tribe of the sidhe and transformed it into the first Thallain, of the Nine Final Battles, of the Triumph Casque of Sorrows, of the shattering of its key into nine pieces by the Red King, and of the establishment of the kingdoms of the Five Beasts of the Dreaming. It would also tell us of the Compact between the fae and humans. And it will tell us more on the Heron Women and Crawfish Men, of the twin of Arike.<br /> <br /> Small titbits and fragments of the Green Compendium (the one which tells not what happened but what could have happened) may even narrate the quest of Lord Gamine to free Arcadia and the Court of High King Ardlanth from the Darkening Curse, and the tyranny of his regent, Bernard Assjack. It could tell us of the rebellion of Prince Yrtalien, and of his subsequent exile.<br /> <br /> This book would be illustrated by Rebecca Guay, Melissa Uran, and Tony Diterlizzi, of course.<br /> <br /> Would you second this wish, this dream?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","user":"mattboggan","date":". 12-30-2015, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T10:36:02-08:00","id":796895,"title":"","content":"I am agree with you. We need something like that. This could also sky rocket the kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T16:50:56-08:00","id":797078,"title":"","content":"Yes! I'd put in some money for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T17:38:02-08:00","id":797090,"title":"","content":"Compendium just sounds.. so.. boring? I know its correct but it doesn't sound historical or poetic. If this is going to be the Changeling's book of Nod, as the book of nod looks to the bible I say look to the epics, The Invasion cycle, Beowulf, the Illiad. Mythic history and poetry intertwinned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:35:33-08:00","id":797290,"title":"","content":"I should really read futher in the forums before posting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10388,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10388-madfox","user":"MadFox","date":". 12-31-2015, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10388-madfox","name":"MadFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T00:36:19-08:00","id":798149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/796872-c-td20-the-black-compendium-what-a-strectch-goal-it-would-be?p=797090#post797090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compendium just sounds.. so.. boring? I know its correct but it doesn't sound historical or poetic. If this is going to be the Changeling's book of Nod, as the book of nod looks to the bible I say look to the epics, The Invasion cycle, Beowulf, the Illiad. Mythic history and poetry intertwinned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly!<br /> <br /> Don't be fooled: the fae love to hide their most secret treasures behind an appearance of normalcy.<br /> <br /> In fact, truth to be told, I don't think that &quot;compendium&quot; is boring. The word, with its Latin sounding, directly evokes compilations of old lore, painfully and patiently gathered by dedicated scholars who worked in windy and cold monasteries but illustrated them with splendid artwork (think Book of Kells). It also evokes the compilations that folklorists love to do, gathering all their lore about the fae in one place (in French, we have the word &quot;elficologiste&quot; which was invented by the so self-proclaimed Pierre Dubois, author of three wondrous encyclopedia of fae -- see here: <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/100631.The_Great_Encyclopedia_Of_Faeries?ac=1&amp;from_search=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/...&amp;from_search=1</a>).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T05:29:23-08:00","id":798212,"title":"","content":"I would *love* to see a Book of Nod style book for Changeling! I've been wanting one since before Changeling made the move to Arthaus.... &gt;_&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":".  Spelling 01-02-2016, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T17:58:17-08:00","id":798517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/796872-c-td20-the-black-compendium-what-a-strectch-goal-it-would-be?p=798149#post798149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, exactly!<br /> <br /> Don't be fooled: the fae love to hide their most secret treasures behind an appearance of normalcy.<br /> <br /> In fact, truth to be told, I don't think that &quot;compendium&quot; is boring. The word, with its Latin sounding, directly evokes compilations of old lore, painfully and patiently gathered by dedicated scholars who worked in windy and cold monasteries but illustrated them with splendid artwork (think Book of Kells). It also evokes the compilations that folklorists love to do, gathering all their lore about the fae in one place (in French, we have the word &quot;elficologiste&quot; which was invented by the so self-proclaimed Pierre Dubois, author of three wondrous encyclopedia of fae -- see here: <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/100631.The_Great_Encyclopedia_Of_Faeries?ac=1&amp;from_search=1\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/...&amp;from_search=1</a>).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand this, but emotionally am not big on Compendium. I know it has a glorious and varied history but it feels to me if a gaming company puts out something called a Compendium I'm not going to feel its a Fluff book vs a gaming book. THis is entirely personal preference.<br /> <br /> OF course I don't have a better word, but I'd love to see it start out as an Epic poem, then Medieval chronicle, then an elizabethan play and so on.. Each event moved forward becoming a different historical style of art as time passes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T18:31:39-08:00","id":798537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/796872-c-td20-the-black-compendium-what-a-strectch-goal-it-would-be?p=798517#post798517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I understand this, but emotionally am not big on Compendium. I know it has a glorious and varied history but it feels to me if a gaming company puts out something called a Compendium I'm not going to feel its a Fluff book vs a gaming book. THis is entirely personal preference.<br /> <br /> OF course I don't have a better word, but I'd love to see it start out as an Epic poem, then Medieval chronicle, then an elizabethan play and so on.. Each event moved forward becoming a different historical style of art as time passes.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be done well, such a book needs stellar writing. Of all of them, Revelations of the Dark Mother was best, but I don't think it's up to handling Elizabethan drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 01-03-2016, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T19:27:13-08:00","id":798580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/796872-c-td20-the-black-compendium-what-a-strectch-goal-it-would-be?p=798537#post798537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be done well, such a book needs a stellar writing. Of all of them, Revelations of the Dark Mother was best, but I don't think it's up to handling Elizabethan drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say there were broadly two types of artifact book. Nod/Revelations/Fragments/DOF which are all variant takes on biblical books. Then you have SIlver Record and Fragile path which try to do something different, they are a diverse collection of stories and styles. I think one that follows the Fragile path method would work better for changeling because there are so many different voices to tell different tales.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T01:22:35-08:00","id":799157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/796872-c-td20-the-black-compendium-what-a-strectch-goal-it-would-be?p=798580#post798580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say there were broadly two types of artifact book. Nod/Revelations/Fragments/DOF which are all variant takes on biblical books. Then you have SIlver Record and Fragile path which try to do something different, they are a diverse collection of stories and styles. I think one that follows the Fragile path method would work better for changeling because there are so many different voices to tell different tales.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. The Biblical style isn't very appropriate. I also think it probably won't be on a level with Elizabethan drama and verse, but then I don't think it needs to be.<br /> <br /> There are older lays, epics, romances and ballads which might actually be better models anyway. These often exist now in translation, as many were written in French or Middle English, and that gives a good 'in' for both a writer and reader, because it allows for a more contemporary/accessible style of language. Contemporary translations of Beowulf, for instance, are rather plainspeaking but still poetic, and are much easier to read as a result.<br /> <br /> Elizabethan English, meanwhile, is dense but still pretty much the same language we use now, so there's no excuse for a 'translation' and therefore I think it will be a much harder read for a gaming product.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the older texts would feel more authentic anyway. Fae history is ancient, so you'd expect something that extends back at least as far as the Middle Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T10:11:09-08:00","id":799684,"title":"","content":"Actually, the inspiration for this kind of book would be naturally the four Irish mythological cycles, with their stories of Gods and Fighting Men : <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/586913.Gods_and_Fighting_Men\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/...d_Fighting_Men</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T10:13:19-08:00","id":799685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/796872-c-td20-the-black-compendium-what-a-strectch-goal-it-would-be?p=799157#post799157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. The Biblical style isn't very appropriate. I also think it probably won't be on a level with Elizabethan drama and verse, but then I don't think it needs to be.<br /> <br /> There are older lays, epics, romances and ballads which might actually be better models anyway. These often exist now in translation, as many were written in French or Middle English, and that gives a good 'in' for both a writer and reader, because it allows for a more contemporary/accessible style of language. Contemporary translations of Beowulf, for instance, are rather plainspeaking but still poetic, and are much easier to read as a result.<br /> <br /> Elizabethan English, meanwhile, is dense but still pretty much the same language we use now, so there's no excuse for a 'translation' and therefore I think it will be a much harder read for a gaming product.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the older texts would feel more authentic anyway. Fae history is ancient, so you'd expect something that extends back at least as far as the Middle Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fae history is an evolving thing.having what first or second generation changelings have to say using more resseance style works for me and I am not asking for someone to write a whole damn play in the shattering but an except from it like Mercutio's death monologue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/796872-c-td20-the-black-compendium-what-a-strectch-goal-it-would-be?p=799684#post799684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the inspiration for this kind of book would be naturally the four Irish mythological cycles, with their stories of Gods and Fighting Men : <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/586913.Gods_and_Fighting_Men\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/...d_Fighting_Men</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Or.. Homer. or the Eddas, or the Tale of igor's Campaign. or Medieval Romances and Chronicles, or 1001 arabian nights... or the Mahabarata or Romance of the Three Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> It would be nice to see more nonceltic views in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 01-03-2016, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"